{"chunk_id": "f45ee4ceeb50", "text": "Hanuman, recognizing Rama and Lakshmana as noble warriors, decides they should meet Sugriva, the exiled monkey king. Dropping his disguise, he carries the brothers across the mountains and introduces them to Sugriva on Mount Rishyamuka. Hanuman explains Rama\u2019s story\u2014his exile and the abduction of Sita by Ravana\u2014and urges Sugriva to form an alliance. Sugriva eagerly agrees, seeing great fortune in Rama\u2019s friendship. The two solemnize their pact before a sacred fire, circling it and pledging mutual loyalty: Rama will kill Bali, the brother who stole Sugriva\u2019s wife and kingdom, while Sugriva will help find Sita. Their bond is sealed with warmth and trust. At that very moment, ominous omens appear\u2014Sita\u2019s eye twitches, as do Sugriva\u2019s and Ravana\u2019s\u2014foreshadowing the vast conflict that this alliance will unleash.\nHanuman brings Rama and Lakshmana to Sugriva, who forms a fire\u2011witnessed alliance with Rama, promising mutual help against Bali and in the search for Sita.\nThemes: alliance and friendship, mutual aid, exile and injustice, oath before fire, foreshadowing omens", "vector": [0.011439064517617226, -0.03767060115933418, -0.0022707446478307247, -0.0012717508943751454, -0.011720188893377781, 0.02827303111553192, -0.004655277822166681, -0.0014934706268832088, -0.01631857268512249, -0.030789759010076523, 0.00536812748759985, 0.0007053197477944195, 0.011198101565241814, 0.004738945513963699, -0.00220213714055717, -0.008654599077999592, 0.05153937637805939, -0.015247623436152935, 0.022155238315463066, -0.017443068325519562, -0.00454483600333333, -0.01840692013502121, -0.011445757932960987, -0.001999660860747099, -0.016198089346289635, 0.0066131046041846275, 0.018165957182645798, -0.03421679139137268, 0.02720208279788494, -0.009698773734271526, -0.004628503695130348, -0.010582306422293186, -0.002158629707992077, 0.005692758597433567, -0.017978541553020477, -0.002904946682974696, -0.